  CVE-2026-3931|2026-03-11T22:16:35.803|2026-03-13T15:41:38.623|8.8|HIGH|CWE-122|N/A|false|Heap buffer overflow in Skia in Google Chrome prior to 146.0.7680.71 allowed a remote attacker to perform out of bounds memory access via a crafted HTML page. (Chromium security severity: Medium)|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-3931
