  CVE-2026-27262|2026-03-11T01:16:57.110|2026-03-11T14:50:28.597|5.4|MEDIUM|CWE-79|N/A|false|Adobe Experience Manager versions 6.5.23 and earlier are affected by a stored Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability that could be abused by an attacker to inject malicious scripts into vulnerable form fields. Malicious JavaScript may be executed in a victim’s browser when they browse to the page containing the vulnerable field.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27262
  CVE-2026-27261|2026-03-11T01:16:56.937|2026-03-16T14:18:59.543|0.0|NONE|N/A|N/A|false|Rejected reason: This CVE ID was issued in error by its CVE Numbering Authority.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27261
